    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"Graph.hyper_wiener_index - EdgeCase\",\n    \"isPartOf\": {\"@type\": \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/Graph.hyper_wiener_index.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.hyper_wiener_index()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Calculate the hyper-Wiener index of an undirected graph.\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.hyper_wiener_index()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Calculate the hyper-Wiener index of an undirected graph.\ntitle: >-\n  [Graph.hyper_wiener_index()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n  .doc-label-method}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: Calculate the hyper-Wiener index of an undirected graph.\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nCalculate the hyper-Wiener index of an undirected graph.\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L84847-L84942){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\nGraph.hyper_wiener_index(weighted=None)\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\n![Hyper-Wiener index](../assets/graphs/hyper-wiener-index.light.svg){.lightbox fig-alt=\"The six-node graph of the Wiener index figure and a card that groups its 15 node pairs by shortest-path distance, each pair adding half of d times d plus one: 6 pairs at distance 1 add 1 each, 6 at 2 add 3, 2 at 3 add 6, and 1 at 4 adds 10. The sum is the hyper-Wiener index 46.0, against a Wiener index of 28.\" width=\"100%\"}\n\nThe hyper-Wiener index (Randić, 1993) refines the Wiener index by also summing squared\ndistances, so far-apart pairs weigh more heavily:\n\n`WW(G) = ½ Σ_{u < v} (d(u, v) + d(u, v)²)`\n\nEquivalently, `½ d (d + 1)` is the number of sub-paths of a shortest path of length\n`d`, so the index counts, over all pairs, the paths contained in their shortest paths\n(Klein, Lukovits and Gutman, 1995). Like `wiener_index()`, it is a topological\ndescriptor in chemistry, where it correlates with boiling points and other properties\nof molecules; the square term makes it more sensitive to a molecule's elongation.\n:::\n\n## Parameters {.doc-parameters}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code>[weighted]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [bool | None]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   If `True`, edge weights (`1` where missing) are the distances. If `False`, every edge\n    has distance `1`. If `None` (default), follows whether the graph was created as\n    weighted.\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [float]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   The hyper-Wiener index. Returns `0.0` for graphs with fewer than two nodes and\n    infinity (`float('inf')`) for disconnected graphs.\n:::\n\n## Raises {.doc-raises}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [ValueError]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   If the graph is directed.\n:::\n\n## Technical Notes {.doc-technical-notes}\n\nThe sum runs over unordered pairs, as in Randić's and Klein et al.'s definition and in\n`wiener_index()`, which gives the values tabulated in the chemistry literature\n(15 for the 4-node path, butane's carbon skeleton). NetworkX's `hyper_wiener_index()`\nsums over ordered pairs while keeping the factor of one half, so its values are\nexactly twice these (30 for the 4-node path). Distances come from a breadth-first\nsearch from every node, or Dijkstra's algorithm with `weighted=True`, in\n$O(V(V + E))$ or $O(V(V + E) \\log V)$ time.\n\n## See Also {.doc-see-also}\n\n[](`~wiener_index`) \n\n:   The plain sum of distances.\n\n[](`~kirchhoff_index`) \n\n:   Sum resistance distances instead.\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\nEach pair at distance `d` adds `d (d + 1) / 2`, so on a path of four nodes the three\npairs at `1` add `1` each, the two at `2` add `3` each, and the ends `6`, for `15`:\n\n::: {#ccbc1663 .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\npath = ec.Graph.from_edges([(\"A\", \"B\"), (\"B\", \"C\"), (\"C\", \"D\")])\n\npath.wiener_index(), path.hyper_wiener_index()\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```\n(10.0, 15.0)\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n### Long and compact molecules\n\n`molecules()` holds the graphs of seven small molecules, one node per atom (leaving out\nthe hydrogens) and one edge per bond. The squared distances weigh far-apart atoms more,\nso the index tells long molecules from compact ones more sharply than the Wiener index.\nFrom isobutane to butane, whose four carbons form a chain rather than a branch, the\nWiener index rises by 11% and the hyper-Wiener index by 25%:\n\n::: {#2140af04 .cell execution_count=2}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport polars as pl\n\nmolecules = ec.molecules()\n\npl.DataFrame(\n    {\n        \"molecule\": list(molecules),\n        \"wiener\": [g.wiener_index() for g in molecules.values()],\n        \"hyper_wiener\": [\n            g.hyper_wiener_index() for g in molecules.values()\n        ],\n    }\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}\n```{=html}\n<div><style>\n.dataframe > thead > tr,\n.dataframe > tbody > tr {\n  text-align: right;\n  white-space: pre-wrap;\n}\n</style>\n<small>shape: (7, 3)</small><table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\"><thead><tr><th>molecule</th><th>wiener</th><th>hyper_wiener</th></tr><tr><td>str</td><td>f64</td><td>f64</td></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>&quot;benzene&quot;</td><td>27.0</td><td>42.0</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;cyclohexane&quot;</td><td>27.0</td><td>42.0</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;ethanol&quot;</td><td>4.0</td><td>5.0</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;dimethyl_ether&quot;</td><td>4.0</td><td>5.0</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;butane&quot;</td><td>10.0</td><td>15.0</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;isobutane&quot;</td><td>9.0</td><td>12.0</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;caffeine&quot;</td><td>258.0</td><td>565.0</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n::: {#5d14d8b7 .cell execution_count=3}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nmolecules[\"caffeine\"].plot(\n    color_by=\"element\", label_by=\"label\", seed=1\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=3}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-theme\" style=\"display:contents\"><style class=\"ec-theme-vars\">:where(.ec-theme){--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){.ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}}:is(html.quarto-light, body.quarto-light, html[data-bs-theme=\"light\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"true\"], body.vscode-light, body.vscode-high-contrast-light, html[theme=\"light\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f